    "organizationActivities": "Several student organizations are available. The deanship of Students offer a variety of activities to support students and improve learning environment as well as wellness.",
    "setting": "https://de.rcm.upr.edu/vida-estudiantil",
    "housing": null,
    "supportSystems": "The University of Puerto Rico- School of Medicine believes that diversity and inclusion are \nfundamental elements to provide an enriching environment for our students, residents, faculty, and \nacademic administrators. The School of Medicine is committed to actively participating in all efforts \ntoward recruiting, enrolling, employing, appointing, and retaining a diverse group of students, faculty, \nand academic administrators; diversity is broadly defined as characteristics that strengthen and enrich our academic milieu, in alignment with our mission and values.\nThe School of Medicine acknowledges the diversity of the Puerto Rican society, thrives for an \nequitable representation of that diversity in its academic community, and will encourage and \nsupport its leaders, the departments, the academic programs, students, residents, faculty, and \nacademic administrators to promote inclusion, respect, and culturally competent \ncommunication.",
    "supportSystemsForDisabilities": null,
    "wellnessPrograms": "Mission\n\nInspire and educate medical students, residents and students of biomedical sciences of the School of Medicine with the purpose that they develop the importance of taking over their health and well-being. Provide services, workshops and resources that promote self-care strategies, self-reflection in order to prevent and manage anxiety to avoid burnout and other emotional responses.\n\nVision\n\nDevelop a wellness program that guides and encourages biomedical science students, residents, and medical students to be aware of their physical, mental, emotional, and spiritual needs. Through the different activities, workshops and interventions, it is expected that students can acquire healthy skills and practices that contribute to well-being in the process of reaching their academic and personal goals.",
    "campusCulture": "We strive to provide an inclusive, supportive, and safe learning environment by promoting personal and professional development. We are committed to the health and well-being of our enrolled students. Many student organizations and interest groups are vital to a robust student life experience. These include diversity, community service, and nearly every medical specialty. An atmosphere of respect and tolerance is expected at all times. We will always ensure that our students' voices are heard.",
